show markdown "Overall view" a11h18                                            {tileTab: "OverallView"} with  """
### Documentation

__Forecasting Quality__:

Forecasted items: number of items in scope for which a sales forecast is made

Accuracy in 95% interval: accuracy of the quantile 95 demand scenario, i.e. the scenario which covers 95% of all future plausible demand scenarios.
An overshoot means an overall over forecast, while an undershoot means an overall under forecast.

__Forecast confidence index:__

The forecast confidence index shows if the forecast model correctly fits with the past:

🟢🟢🟢🟢🟢: model fits with the past sales within a +- 5% range

🟢🟢🟢⚫⚫: model fits with the past sales within a +- 8% range

🟢⚫⚫⚫⚫: model fits with the past sales within a range > 8%

See our [forecast page](https://go.lokad.com/d/68002/) for more details

__Categories__:

To forecast: link to the associated forecast tab of the given category

Category: category name

%Turnover: category's proportion of the overall turnover

Turnover L365 d: category's turnover over the last 365 days

Turnover N365 d: category's turnover expected for the next 365 days

Overall Trend: category's expected trend on the next 365 days (ratio of: Turnover N365 d / Turnover L365 d - 1)

__Sales forecast (net amount)__: displays overall past sales amount and overall forecasted future average demand amount, as well as a likely and a plausible area

"""

show markdown "Category view" a11h16                                            {tileTab: "CategoryView"} with  """
### Documentation

__Category Overview__:

% Turnover: category's proportion of the overall turnover

Turnover L365 d: category's turnover over the last 365 days

Turnover N365 d: category's turnover expected for the next 365 days

Trend: category's expected trend on the next 365 days (ratio of: Turnover N365 d / Turnover L365 d - 1)

__Forecasting Quality__:

Forecasted items: number of items of the category in scope for which a sales forecast is made

__Trend for current Turnover__: displays the category's turnover over the last 365 days depending on the trend on the next 365 days. This bar chart helps
understand which part of the overall current turnover will increase or decrease in the future

__NetAmount__: displays category's past sales amount and category's forecasted future average demand amount, as well as a likely and a plausible area

"""

show markdown "Item view" a29h36                                            {tileTab: "ItemView"} with  """
### Documentation

__Category's pareto__: displays the x top best sellers and the proportion of the overall turnover they represent. In dark orange are shown
the specific items displayed below and for which a specific focus is made

__Overrule Quantities - over next 10 weeks__: allows one to manually change the average forecasted demand of every reference from all categories over the next 10 weeks. Once a change is made,
one needs to relaunch the dashboard clicking

Sku: reference code

Name: reference name

Category: name of the category

Week N+x: average forecasted demand of a reference for a given week. Can be changed by the user

__Reference focus__:

Magnifying glass icon: link to the item inspector dashboard which displays all information of the given reference

Life cycle: life cycle of the reference, either new if launched less than 365 days ago, discontinued or unchanged if not new nor discontinued

L365 d: category's sold units over the last 365 days

N365 d: category's sold units over the next 365 days

Trend: category's expected trend on the next 365 days (ratio of: N365 d / L365 d - 1)

Avg LT: reference average supplier LeadTime

Reorder Cycle: reference average reorder frequency

Demand Quantity: displays reference past sales and reference forecasted future average demand, as well as a likely and a plausible area

Demand to cover (Responsibility window): demand forecasted quantity distribution over the responsibility window (in dark red), i.e. a reorder cycle period in a supplier LeadTime period

"""
